course: dictionary
lesson: 2321
title: A crossroads: where roads meet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A crossroads is a place where two roads meet and cross each other. Read the sentence: «Laws are made by a country's lawmakers, and everyone must follow them; traffic lights are a law that stops crashes at crossroads.» The clues are traffic lights and crashes, so a crossroads must be a busy place where roads cross, and it needs rules to keep people safe.
explain: The word also has a second meaning. «At a crossroads» means you have reached a time when you must make an important choice, like a traveller who must pick which road to take.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Traffic lights stop crashes at places where two roads meet and cross» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
fact: A crossroads is a place where two roads meet and cross each other.
fact: The word is usually written crossroads, and it is used for one place and for many places.
fact: «At a crossroads» means at a time when you must make an important choice.
fact: At a crossroads, look both ways and use the crossing, and wait for the green signal before you cross.
exercise: «Traffic lights are a law that stops crashes at crossroads.» Where do the traffic lights stop crashes? | On a quiet path with no cars | *At a place where two roads meet and cross | Inside a shop | In the middle of a field
exercise: Maya is at a crossroads in her story. She can go left to the forest or right to the river. What does «at a crossroads» mean here? | She is crossing a busy road | She is lost in a shop | She is very tired | *She must make an important choice
exercise: What should you do at a busy crossroads? | Run across quickly with your eyes closed | Cross whenever you feel like it | Stand in the middle and wait | *Look both ways and wait for the green signal
test: Which meaning fits «a busy crossroads»? | A large grassy field | *A place where two roads meet and cross | A type of bus | A small shop
test: Dad says, «We're at a crossroads with our holiday plans.» What does he mean? | We have lost the map | We are crossing the road | We are very tired | *We must make an important choice
exam: «We reached the busy crossroads and turned left.» What does crossroads mean? | A car park for buses | *A place where two roads meet and cross | A tunnel under a river | A path through a forest
